  "published": "2026-11-08T13:35:52.603Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.12.1 fixes the online session when an app validates another license while it runs, for example a trial that becomes a paid license. No API change.\n\n- The session moves to the license validated last. Before, the heartbeat kept sending the first license, the new license had no session, and the app could show \"Session lost and reconnect failed: Invalid session token\" until the first session timed out.\n- The previous license's session ends on the server, so its seat is free at once.\n- Re-validating the license that is already connected keeps its session instead of reconnecting.\n\n1.12.0 adds IntelliSense documentation and removes two unused dependencies. No API or behavior change.\n\n- The package now includes XML documentation for the public API, so Visual Studio, VS Code and Rider show descriptions for LicenseClient, LicenseClientOptions, the validation results and the other public types.\n- LicenPro.SDK no longer depends on Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder or Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions, which it never used. If your app calls IConfiguration.Get<T>(), GetValue<T>() or Bind(), or uses IServiceCollection, and got those packages only through LicenPro.SDK, add them to your project.\n\nUpgrading from 1.8.x: also read the 1.11.0 release notes (public key built into the app, SignatureMismatch, rebuild).\n\nLanguages: .NET and VB.NET use this package. The native library for Python and other languages gets the same fix.",
